    "title": "Concept: Threshold values on cumulative frequency graphs",
    "explanation": "<p class=\"text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground\">A threshold is a specific value on the horizontal (data) axis of a cumulative frequency graph. To find how many data values fall below or equal to this threshold, you read vertically up to the curve, then horizontally across to the vertical (frequency) axis. To find how many data values fall above the threshold, subtract the cumulative frequency at this threshold from the total number of data points.</p>",
