    "explanation": "<p class=\"text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground\">When two or more cumulative frequency graphs are plotted on the same axes, comparisons can be made about their distributions. By examining the medians, quartiles, and interquartile ranges (IQRs), we learn which distribution has higher typical values, greater spread, or more consistency. Steeper sections of the curve indicate many data points clustered in a narrow range, while flatter sections show data spread over a wider range.</p>",
