    "title": "Concept: Reading estimates from cumulative frequency curves",
    "explanation": "<p class=\"text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground\">Key estimates from cumulative frequency graphs include the median, lower quartile (Q1), upper quartile (Q3), and the interquartile range (IQR). These are found by reading horizontally from 25%, 50%, and 75% of the total frequency respectively, then vertically down to the data axis. The median divides the data into two halves, Q1 covers the lower 25%, and Q3 the upper 25%. The IQR, calculated as Q3 minus Q1, measures the spread of the middle 50% of the data.</p>",
